Package: mkbbs
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: @ARCH@
Section: comm
Priority: optional
Maintainer: @MAINTAINER@
Installed-Size: @SIZE@
Depends: libc6 (>= 2.34), adduser
Provides: mkdraw
Conflicts: mkdraw
Replaces: mkdraw
Recommends: zip, unzip, libssl3t64 | libssl3, stunnel4, bubblewrap
Suggests: openssh-server | dropbear-bin, dosemu2, curl
Homepage: https://github.com/mythicalkingdom/mkbbs
Description: MK BBS: a bulletin board system with FidoNet and QWK networking
 A Free Pascal conversion of the DOS MK BBS toolkit.  It has a Telnet, raw,
 WebSocket and SSH-fronted listener (mklisten), message and file areas, a
 menu system, an offline mail door (QWK / QWKE), a FidoNet tosser with TIC file
 echoes and file requests, a binkp mailer interface, QWK network passes (Telnet
 scripts, FTP, FTPS or your own programs), DOS door support through dosemu2,
 and the configuration, user and file editors.
 .
 It includes mkdraw (the ANSI screen editor) and mkcat with their manual
 pages, the same programs as the package mkdraw, which it replaces: install
 one or the other.
 .
 The package installs the programs, the systemd unit of the listener (not
 started: edit /etc/mkbbs/mklisten.json first), the language files and the
 documentation.  The BBS directory itself (configuration, menus, message
 bases) is made with mkconfig; see /usr/share/doc/mkbbs/GETTING-STARTED.md.
